From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:24:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mt6797-spm-sleep: acknowledge SYS_CIRQ when a
 period ends

spm_cirq_disable() replays the recorded edges into the GIC and disables
SYS_CIRQ, but leaves its status set. The status is acknowledged only by
the next period's spm_cirq_enable(), which runs after the kick. A program
reused from IM (sodi_im_reuse) reaches its wake check within microseconds
of the kick, sees the previous period's status as a wake and returns at
once. In stage D5r every second period ended this way.

Acknowledge every status word right after the flush, as the vendor's exit
does.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
index 10fd72c04..09d27b575 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
@@ -799,7 +799,13 @@ static void spm_cirq_enable(void)
 	       (level ? 0 : CIRQ_EDGE), s.cirq + CIRQ_CON);
 }
 
-/* Before the GIC is restored: note, replay and disable (mt_cirq_flush) */
+/*
+ * Before the GIC is restored: note, replay, acknowledge and disable
+ * (mt_cirq_flush). Without the acknowledgement the status recorded in this
+ * period stays set until the next period's spm_cirq_enable, which runs after
+ * the kick; a resident program reaches its wake check before that and ends
+ * at once on the stale status (D5r).
+ */
 static void spm_cirq_disable(void)
 {
 	unsigned int w;
@@ -807,6 +813,8 @@ static void spm_cirq_disable(void)
 	for (w = 0; w < CIRQ_WORDS; w++)
 		s.cirq_sta[w] = readl(s.cirq + CIRQ_STA + 4 * w);
 	writel(readl(s.cirq + CIRQ_CON) | CIRQ_FLUSH, s.cirq + CIRQ_CON);
+	for (w = 0; w < CIRQ_WORDS; w++)
+		writel(~0u, s.cirq + CIRQ_ACK + 4 * w);
 	writel(readl(s.cirq + CIRQ_CON) & ~(CIRQ_EN | CIRQ_EDGE), s.cirq + CIRQ_CON);
 	for (w = 0; w < CIRQ_WORDS; w++)
 		writel(~0u, s.cirq + CIRQ_MASK_SET + 4 * w);
-- 
